# Dev defaults for `vite dev`. Committed on purpose: it contains no secret, and
# without it the UI silently falls back to fixture mode.
#
# An empty base makes `frontClient` use same-origin paths, which the Vite dev
# proxy (see vite.config.ts) forwards to the Front server. Going cross-origin
# instead would fail: the stdlib Python server sends no CORS headers, so the
# browser's /health probe is blocked and the client honestly reports itself as
# read-only fixture mode.
VITE_AUREL_FRONT_BASE=
